      <main>
        <h2>Privacy Policy</h2>
        <p>Last Updated: January 2026</p>

        <p>
          At Bookmore, we value your privacy and are committed to protecting your personal information. This Privacy
          Policy explains how we collect, use, and safeguard your data when you visit our website or make a purchase.
          <br>

          By using our website, you agree to the practices described in this Privacy Policy.
        </p>

        <p>
          <strong>1. Information We Collect</strong>
          When you visit Bookmore, we may collect the following information: <br>
          Your name <br>
          Email address <br>
          Shipping and billing address <br>
          Phone number <br>
          Payment information (processed securely by our payment provider) <br>
          Order history <br>
          Information about how you use our website (such as pages visited and products viewed)
        </p>

        <p>
          <strong>2. How We Use Your Information</strong>
          We use your information to: <br>
          Process and deliver your orders <br>
          Provide customer support <br>
          Send order confirmations and shipping updates <br>
          Improve our website and services <br>
          Respond to your enquiries <br>
          Notify you about special offers and promotions (only if you choose to receive them)
        </p>

        <p>
          <strong>3. Payment Security</strong>
          Your payment information is processed using secure payment systems. <br>

          Bookmore does not store your full credit or debit card details on our servers. <br>

          All transactions are protected using industry-standard encryption technologies.
        </p>

        <p>
          <strong>4. Cookies</strong>
          Our website uses cookies to improve your browsing experience. <br>

          Cookies help us: <br>

          Remember your preferences <br>
          Keep items in your shopping cart <br>
          Analyse website traffic <br>
          Improve website performance <br>

          You can disable cookies in your browser settings at any time, although some features of the website may not
          function properly.
        </p>

        <p>
          <strong>5. Sharing Your Information</strong>
          We respect your privacy. <br>

          Bookmore does not sell, rent, or trade your personal information to third parties. <br>

          We may share limited information only with trusted service providers who help us: <br>

          Process payments <br>
          Deliver orders <br>
          Provide customer support <br>
          Maintain website functionality <br>

          These partners are required to protect your information and use it only for the services they provide.
        </p>

        <p>
          <strong>6. Data Security</strong>
          We take reasonable measures to protect your personal information against unauthorised access, alteration,
          disclosure, or destruction. <br>

          While no online service can guarantee complete security, we continually work to keep your information safe.
        </p>

        <p>
          <strong>7. Your Rights</strong>
          Depending on your location, you may have the right to: <br>

          Access the personal information we hold about you <br>
          Correct inaccurate information <br>
          Request deletion of your personal data <br>
          Withdraw consent for marketing communications <br>
          Request a copy of your stored information <br>

          To exercise any of these rights, please contact our support team.
        </p>

        <p>
          <strong>8. Third-Party Links</strong>
          Our website may contain links to third-party websites. <br>

          Bookmore is not responsible for the privacy practices or content of external websites. We encourage you to
          review their privacy policies before providing any personal information.
        </p>

        <p>
          <strong>9. Children's Privacy</strong>
          Bookmore is not intended for children under the age of 13. <br>

          We do not knowingly collect personal information from children. If we become aware that such information has
          been collected, it will be deleted promptly.
        </p>

        <p>
          <strong>10. Changes to This Privacy Policy</strong>
          We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time to reflect changes in our services or legal requirements.
          <br>

          Any updates will be posted on this page with the revised Last Updated date.
        </p>

        <p>
          <strong>11. Contact Us</strong>
          If you have any questions about this Privacy Policy or how we handle your personal information, please <a
            href="/contacts">contact us</a>.
        </p>

        <p>
          Your Privacy Matters
        </p>

        <p>
          At Bookmore, we're committed to providing a safe, secure, and enjoyable shopping experience. Thank you for
          trusting us with your information.
        </p>

